is *not* a point of inflection for two reasons. First, the function does not change concavity. It's concave up both to the left and to the right of $x=0.$ Second, the tangent line does not exist at this point.\n\n- The point $x=1$ is *not* a point of inflection. Although the graph changes concavity from concave up to concave down at $x=1,$   the function is not defined at this point, so the tangent line does not exist either.\n\nTherefore, the point of inflection is $x=-1$ only." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038344/state.json" "file_sha256" "7b2eb7014625d312e0ec0bc0219751c7ec81df838e5dd38e6d70674cecd0bfe4"} {"question" "q-127112" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038344/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0ee3ddc13c2edc963e9bd9e50859c473c32a745668b82400b5d0a055d71c2994"} {"question" "q-127112" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038344/state.json" "file_sha256" "7b2eb7014625d312e0ec0bc0219751c7ec81df838e5dd38e6d70674cecd0bfe4"} {"question" "q-127112" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "$x=-1$ and $x=0$"] ["text" "$x=-1$ and $x=1$"] ["text" "$x=-1$ only"] ["text" "$x=0$ and $x=1$"] ["text" "$x=1$ only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038344/state.json" "file_sha256" "7b2eb7014625d312e0ec0bc0219751c7ec81df838e5dd38e6d70674cecd0bfe4"} {"question" "q-127112" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "$x=-1$ only"] "category" "ma_successfu