der for the graph to change concavity, the value of the second derivative ${f}^{″}(x)$ must switch sign. So, we are looking for points where the graph of ${f}^{″}(x)$ crosses the $x$-axis.\n\nWe can see that the graph $y={f}^{″}(x)$ crosses the $x$-axis at $x=0$ and $x=4.$ \n\nTherefore, $f(x)$ has points of inflection at $x=0$ and $x=4.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038344/state.json" "file_sha256" "7b2eb7014625d312e0ec0bc0219751c7ec81df838e5dd38e6d70674cecd0bfe4"} {"question" "q-31213" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038344/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0ee3ddc13c2edc963e9bd9e50859c473c32a745668b82400b5d0a055d71c2994"} {"question" "q-31213" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038344/state.json" "file_sha256" "7b2eb7014625d312e0ec0bc0219751c7ec81df838e5dd38e6d70674cecd0bfe4"} {"question" "q-31213" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "x=0"] ["text" "$x=-4$ and $x=4$"] ["text" "$x=-4,$ $x=0,$ and $x=4$"] ["text" "$x=-6$ and $x=-2$"] ["text" "$x=0$ and $x=4$"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038344/state.json" "file_sha256" "7b2eb7014625d312e0ec0bc0219751c7ec81df838e5dd38e6d70674cecd0bfe4"} {"question" "q-31213" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "$x=0$ and $x=4$"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038344/state.json" "f